articles.content_en:
The People's Bank of China shall perform the following functions:
(1) issuing orders and regulations related to the performance of its functions;
(2) formulating and implementing monetary policies according to law;
(3) issuing Renminbi and managing the circulation of Renminbi;
(4) supervising and regulating the interbank lending market and the interbank bond market;
(5) implementing foreign exchange administration and supervising and regulating the interbank foreign exchange market;
(6) supervising and regulating the gold market;
(7) holding, managing and operating the state foreign exchange reserves and gold reserves;
(8) acting as the fiscal agent;
(9) maintaining the normal operation of the payment and clearing systems;
(10) directing and arranging the anti-money laundering work in the financial industry and being responsible for monitoring funds for anti-money laundering;
(11) being responsible for statistics, investigation, analysis and forecasts of the financial industry;
(12) engaging in relevant international financial activities as the central bank of the state;
(13) other functions as prescribed by the State Council.
For the purpose of implementing monetary policies, the People's Bank of China may engage in financial business activities in accordance with the relevant provisions of Chapter IV of this Law.

For the purpose of implementing monetary policies, the People's Bank of China may use the following monetary policy instruments:
(1) requiring banking financial institutions to deposit a required reserve ratio in accordance with the prescribed proportion;
(2) fixing the base interest rates of the central bank;
(3) handling rediscount for banking financial institutions that have opened accounts with the People's Bank of China;
(4) providing loans to commercial banks;
(5) buying and selling government bonds, other government securities and financial bonds and foreign exchange in the open market;
(6) other monetary policy instruments as determined by the State Council.
When using the monetary policy instruments listed in the preceding paragraph for the purpose of implementing monetary policies, the People's Bank of China may prescribe specific conditions and procedures.

The People's Bank of China shall have the power to inspect and supervise the following activities of financial institutions and other units and individuals:
(1) activities relating to the implementation of the regulations on deposit reserve management;
(2) activities relating to special loans of the People's Bank of China;
(3) activities relating to the implementation of the regulations on Renminbi management;
(4) activities relating to the implementation of the regulations on the interbank lending market and interbank bond market management;
(5) activities relating to the implementation of the regulations on foreign exchange management;
(6) activities relating to the implementation of the regulations on gold management;
(7) activities relating to acting as the fiscal agent of the People's Bank of China;
(8) activities relating to the implementation of the regulations on clearing management;
(9) activities relating to the implementation of the regulations on anti-money laundering.
The special loans of the People's Bank of China as mentioned in the preceding paragraph refer to loans decided by the State Council and granted by the People's Bank of China to financial institutions for specific purposes.

Where the People's Bank of China commits any of the following acts, the persons directly in charge and other persons directly responsible shall be given administrative sanctions according to law; if the act constitutes a crime, criminal liability shall be investigated according to law:
(1) providing loans in violation of the provisions of the first paragraph of Article 30 of this Law;
(2) providing guarantees to units or individuals;
(3) using issue funds without authorization.
Where any of the acts listed in the preceding paragraph causes losses, the persons directly in charge and other persons directly responsible shall bear partial or full liability for compensation.
